  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "The Modern Ledger",
    "overview": "A risk register kept like a ledger, not a dashboard template. Figures are posted, never silently overwritten: when a residual score changes, the old figure is struck through in red ink and the new one is posted beside it, on the heat-map cells and in every row that shows a score. The rest of the system stays quiet so that one movement reads.\n\nThe world is a cool, bright ground with white sheets divided by 1px rules. There are no cards-with-shadows, no gradients, no dark mode (light only, chosen for office desktops and projectors in bright rooms). One sans (Geist) carries everything with tabular figures; one ledger-green accent marks actions, the current location and focus; red ink is reserved for adverse movement and destructive actions; four pale rating washes are always paired with the rating word or score. Density is high and fixed: a practitioner scans both 5x5 matrices and the register without scrolling through chrome.",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "Light-only, flat, ruled: depth comes from tonal layers and 1px rules, not shadows.",
      "One sans family with tabular numerals; mono only for hashes and event ids.",
      "One accent (green) for action; red only for adverse; rating washes never stand alone.",
      "One authored motion: posting a figure. Everything else is a 150ms state fade."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The One Voice Rule",
        "body": "Ledger Green appears only on things you can act on, the current nav item, focus and the live/effective signals. Never as decoration or a heading colour. Selection inside a control (segmented option, matrix cell) is solid ink, not green.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Red Ink Rule",
        "body": "Red marks adverse risk movement, failures and destructive actions. It never decorates.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Word-With-Wash Rule",
        "body": "A rating colour never appears without its rating word or numeric score beside or inside it.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Tabular Rule",
        "body": "Every number that can change or be compared (scores, counts, pager totals, axis numbers) is set with tabular figures and right-aligned in tables.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Sentence-Case Rule",
        "body": "Labels and table heads are sentence case at 500 weight; nothing is set in tracked uppercase (the avatar initial is the only uppercase).",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Rules-Not-Shadows Rule",
        "body": "Sections separate by 1px rules and tonal layers. A shadow means focus or state, never altitude.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "**Do** use the posted-figure treatment for any score or count that changes live; it is the system's only authored motion.",
      "**Do** pair every rating wash with its word or score, in cells, badges and the legend.",
      "**Do** separate content with 1px `rule` hairlines and the ground / sheet / sheet-2 layers.",
      "**Do** set changeable numbers tabular and right-aligned.",
      "**Do** keep transitions on hover and focus to 150ms colour, border or shadow fades.",
      "**Do** mark synthetic data with the dashed \"demo data\" tag."
